# .contextignore — files an agent must never spend context reading.
#
# Read by claude-context-optimizer (MIT, github.com/egorfedorov/claude-context-optimizer),
# which blocks `Read` on a match and tells the agent to Grep instead. Same syntax as
# .gitignore.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, beyond saving tokens: `skills/scrooge-delegate` already carries
# the rule "never hand a subagent a task that must read a large or generated file
# (>~30-50 KB, minified/base64/lockfile) — it thrashes a small-context subagent even when
# perfectly specified". That was prose the model had to remember. This file makes it a
# gate. Same "enforce, don't trust the model" move as the constitution's other rules.
#
# Entries are evidence-based: sized against `git ls-files | xargs du -k | sort -rn`
# 2026-08-05, plus the untracked build/tooling dirs actually present in this checkout.
#
# TO ALLOW A BLOCKED READ: delete its line. To search inside a blocked file, use Grep —
# it is not blocked, and it is the right tool for a lockfile or a bundle anyway.

# ── Dependency + build output (never source of truth; regenerate, don't read) ──
node_modules/**
package-lock.json
**/out/**
**/dist/**
coverage/**
*.vsix
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Generated / machine-owned state ───────────────────────────────────────────
# .codegraph is a 33MB SQLite index — query it via the codegraph MCP tools, never read it.
.codegraph/**
.minspec/generated-hashes.json
**/*.generated.*
**/*.snap

# ── Minified or bundled artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map

# ── Binary media (a Read spends tokens and returns nothing useful) ────────────
# Site imagery and extension marketing assets: 800KB+ PNGs at the top of the size list.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.ico
*.webp
*.pdf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.eot
sites/**/img/old/**

# ── Lockfiles of other ecosystems (present or future) ─────────────────────────
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.lock

# ── NOT ignored, deliberately ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# packages/minspec/src/lib/ci-review-templates.ts is 256KB / 2500 lines, the largest
# source file here — but it is hand-maintained source with zero long/base64 lines
# (checked: 0 lines over 200 chars), and the ai-review prompts live in it. Blocking it
# would hide load-bearing logic. Read it with offset/limit instead.
#
# specs/**, docs/**, .minspec/** (except generated-hashes.json) stay readable — they are
# the approvables, and reading them before changing them is the whole methodology.
